  "name": "Conjure Elemental",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "icons/magic/perception/third-eye-blue-red.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You conjure up an elemental to serve you. It manifests in an unoccupied space that you can see within range. The form uses the Conjured Elemental stat block. When you use this creation, choose an element: Air, Earth, Fire, or Water. The creature's form is wreathed in the chosen element, which determines certain traits in its stat block. The creature disappears when it drops to 0 hit points or when the creation ends.\nThe creature is an ally to you and your companions. In combat, the creature shares your initiative count. It obeys your verbal commands (no action required by you). If you don’t issue any, it takes the Dodge action and uses its move to avoid danger.</p><p><strong>At Higher Levels.</strong> When you use this creation with a creation slot of 4th level or higher, use the higher level wherever the creation’s level appears in the stat block.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
